---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import { href, GITHUB_URL } from '../../lib/catalog';
---
<Layout title="How images stay current — daily rebuilds and version bumps" description="Each image family rebuilds daily for Wolfi CVE patches, and upstream releases arrive as reviewed version-bump pull requests.">
  <section>
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href={href('/docs/')}>Docs</a></p>
      <h1 class="section-title">How images stay current</h1>
      <p class="section-sub">Two independent loops: a daily rebuild that picks up Wolfi package fixes, and upstream version bumps that arrive as pull requests.</p>

      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:36px">One workflow per image family</h2>
      <p>
        Every family — PostgreSQL, the CloudNativePG operator, OpenBao, os-shell, DokuWiki, Grafana Image
        Renderer, Cilium and cert-manager — has its own workflow. Routing is the native
        <code class="kv-mono">on.push.paths</code> filter, so a change to one image's directory rebuilds only that
        image, and one family's failure can never cancel another's build.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:36px">Daily rebuilds</h2>
      <p>
        Each workflow runs on its own daily schedule, staggered a few minutes apart from 06:00 UTC. A rebuild
        re-resolves the apko package set against Wolfi, so a CVE fix that lands in Wolfi reaches a published tag
        within a day — without a commit. Each rebuild runs the full pipeline:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>melange compiles the upstream source on native amd64 and arm64 runners;</li>
        <li>apko assembles the image, guarded by a committed lockfile;</li>
        <li>the image's own <code class="kv-mono">test.sh</code> smoke-tests the published image;</li>
        <li>grype scans the published digest;</li>
        <li>cosign signs it — only if the scan has zero findings Low or above;</li>
        <li>this site redeploys with the fresh entry.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:36px">Upstream version bumps</h2>
      <p>
        The <code class="kv-mono">update-versions</code> workflow checks upstream daily (PGDG for each tracked
        PostgreSQL major, GitHub releases for everything else) and opens a pull request bumping
        <code class="kv-mono">version</code> and <code class="kv-mono">sha256</code> in the melange config. Merging
        the PR rebuilds, rescans and resigns only that image, and updates its entry here in place.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">
        Workflows: <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/tree/main/.github/workflows`} rel="noopener">.github/workflows</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
